riscos-mesa: OSMesa contexts drawn by RISC3D, a hardware path.

Where riscos_mesa_pick_renderer says RISC3D, an OSMesa context also gets a
RISC3D context for the same API, and OSMesaMakeCurrent on a buffer RISC3D
can draw into (8 bits a component, OSMesa's colour formats) draws through
it, the frame copied into the program's buffer at glFinish, glFlush,
another MakeCurrent and OSMesaGetColorBuffer. Everything else draws in
software as before. The work is in riscos-mesa's osmesa/risc3d_route.c;
this patch adds the hooks osmesa.c calls (osmesa_riscos.h: strong on RISC
OS, where libOSMesa contains them; weak elsewhere, so the build machine's
libOSMesa draws in software unless a test defines them) and
OSMESA_SOFTWARE_RISCOS, with which EGL keeps its own contexts in software.

